{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02455",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.72,
      "end_seconds": 4.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.93,
      "end_seconds": 14.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "So, of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 18.8,
      "end_seconds": 26.23,
      "duration_seconds": 7.43,
      "text": "Mm, doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.81,
      "end_seconds": 30.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 32.58,
      "end_seconds": 39.94,
      "duration_seconds": 7.36,
      "text": "It's, It's dizziness, doctor. He didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.61,
      "end_seconds": 44.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.19,
      "end_seconds": 49.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "I'd say two weeks, maybe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 50.45,
      "end_seconds": 55.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Right, hm, I'd say more like three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.74,
      "end_seconds": 60.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly two to three weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.91,
      "end_seconds": 64.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, roughly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.43,
      "end_seconds": 69.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "So, rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.71,
      "end_seconds": 73.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "About a four out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.8,
      "end_seconds": 82.28,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 82.38,
      "end_seconds": 90.96,
      "duration_seconds": 8.58,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.76,
      "end_seconds": 112.44,
      "duration_seconds": 19.68,
      "text": "I was getting to that! Oh, um, and being drowsy. About being drowsy, about a three out of ten. Erm, you know, I've had a headache too, for about four days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.17,
      "end_seconds": 134.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Have you had any fever, rash or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.84,
      "end_seconds": 141.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "No, you know, no fever, rash or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.84,
      "end_seconds": 145.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.71,
      "end_seconds": 146.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.08,
      "end_seconds": 151.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.29,
      "end_seconds": 157.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Um, uh, no, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.77,
      "end_seconds": 160.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.48,
      "end_seconds": 164.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.76,
      "end_seconds": 171.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.15,
      "end_seconds": 177.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.04,
      "end_seconds": 184.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.66,
      "end_seconds": 191.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.7,
      "end_seconds": 197.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Alright, any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.97,
      "end_seconds": 204.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "My uncle has high cholesterol. My father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.83,
      "end_seconds": 209.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.42,
      "end_seconds": 223.6,
      "duration_seconds": 13.18,
      "text": "Oh, um, I take febuxostat, 80 milligrams, once a day for the gout. Metoprolol. I take it 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.58,
      "end_seconds": 235.27,
      "duration_seconds": 9.69,
      "text": "I mean, it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.2,
      "end_seconds": 239.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.05,
      "end_seconds": 259.09,
      "duration_seconds": 18.04,
      "text": "Actually, for the seizures, I believe. My daughter sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. I take something called suma... sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, maybe, when needed for my migraines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.02,
      "end_seconds": 265.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.85,
      "end_seconds": 273.93,
      "duration_seconds": 8.08,
      "text": "No, it's at home. I mean, I used to take propranolol, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.76,
      "end_seconds": 277.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.88,
      "end_seconds": 284.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "I had a bunion operation six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.52,
      "end_seconds": 292.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.43,
      "end_seconds": 304.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Yes, gout. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.68,
      "end_seconds": 307.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.97,
      "end_seconds": 312.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.6,
      "end_seconds": 319.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "And besides that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.59,
      "end_seconds": 331.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.8,
      "text": "I've had epilepsy for nearly five years now. Migraines, for nearly five years. I have thin bones, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.3,
      "end_seconds": 340.21,
      "duration_seconds": 7.91,
      "text": "Alright, gout and high blood pressure, that matches what I have here. Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.22,
      "end_seconds": 353.47,
      "duration_seconds": 12.25,
      "text": "Um, you know, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 354.79,
      "end_seconds": 360.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. BP is 118 over 82, pulse 80."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.09,
      "end_seconds": 363.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.51,
      "end_seconds": 369.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.47,
      "end_seconds": 373.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.77,
      "end_seconds": 396.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "Your lips are pink but the whole household feels unwell, and the oxygen reading looks normal but cannot be trusted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.52,
      "end_seconds": 404.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 412.52,
      "end_seconds": 422.55,
      "duration_seconds": 10.03,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. I think we're dealing with possible carbon monoxide poisoning at this stage. A viral illness is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.44,
      "end_seconds": 428.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "Um, do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 430.13,
      "end_seconds": 465.17,
      "duration_seconds": 35.04,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's possible carbon monoxide poisoning, and we'll know more once the a carboxyhaemoglobin blood test is back. I think a carboxyhaemoglobin blood test makes sense here, for possible carbon monoxide poisoning. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. We'll begin with high-flow oxygen, 15 litres per minute, continuous, until reviewed. That should help with carbon monoxide poisoning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 466.89,
      "end_seconds": 497.93,
      "duration_seconds": 31.04,
      "text": "Leave the house now, don't use the boiler, and call the gas emergency number. I'm going to send a referral to the emergency team. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 499.58,
      "end_seconds": 502.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Well, that's fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 503.57,
      "end_seconds": 509.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "Book a review straight away. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 510.98,
      "end_seconds": 516.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Good, uh, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}